This version builds `values` and `stringIndexes` directly from the source field in the member initializer list. The original first default-constructed both vectors and then copy-assigned into them, which is redundant work.

Behavior is unchanged:
- Both members end up as identical copies of the source.
- Any other members are still default-initialized, exactly as before.
- The initializer list does not change construction order, because members are always constructed in declaration order.

```cpp
FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
    : values(field.values), stringIndexes(field.stringIndexes)
{
}
```